Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||12-19-2001||04:20 PM||||I was thinking about ordering a set of 16 inch rims and tires to match.  How will this affect my Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BlackARROW||12-19-2001||05:27 PM||||Other than the look, it'll affect the handling while hard-cornering, slimmer tire will give you better grip, and depending on your mag model, maybe will give better aeration for the brakes.  Maybe it'll be a bit less predictable when about to lose its grip... while drifting - of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'd go for the 16" for the grip and the look  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
Z||000002||gggg-us||12-19-2001||08:29 PM||||What is the biggest tires you can put in a stock fiero?<P>How does lowering affect tire size?<P>------------------<BR>88 4Cyl ... Rebuilding 81 Vette Engine for it now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ToddAsh||12-19-2001||09:39 PM|||| I have 215-50-16 on GT and 215-55-16 on my SE.Big change in handling and they look great.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||12-19-2001||10:37 PM||||You can run 16x8 and 255/50-16's easily on the rear, with the right offset.<P>With that size rear tire, you'd probably want a 215-225 front tire.<p>[This message has been edited by Will (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
